WEB SOURCE (the specification) — components/FormatterPrefsBridge.tsx (+ the libs it binds)
  FormatterPrefsBridge.tsx — mounts near the React root and renders `null`. It is a side-effect-only bridge that
    keeps the module-level number-format globals in sync with the persisted user settings:
      • useSettingsQuery() (the `['settings']` query) + useQueryClient().
      • locale  = resolveLocale(settings.locale)            // lib/locale.ts: non-empty(after trim) tag, else "en-US"
      • decimals = settings.decimal_precision ?? 2
      • useEffect([settings]) applies setGlobalLocale(locale) / setGlobalPrecision(decimals) with a de-dupe:
        write only when the value !== the bridge's last-written value AND !== the current global; on the first
        resolve, record the observed value even when no write was needed (lastLocale/lastDecimals refs).
      • mounting it creates a PERMANENT `['settings']` subscriber so cross-tab invalidations always refetch.
      • useEffect: subscribe((msg) => { if (msg.type === TOPICS.SETTINGS_CHANGED) qc.invalidateQueries(['settings']) }).
  numberFormat.ts globals — `_globalLocale='en-US'`, `_globalPrecision=2`; setGlobalLocale empties to "en-US";
    setGlobalPrecision clamps Math.max(0, Math.min(20, decimals)); getGlobalLocale/getGlobalPrecision read them.
  Render output — `null` (no JSX, no t() keys; the surface is anonymous).

