PARITY MAPPING (web -> Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex)
  useSettingsQuery / useQueryClient     -> P1/S8 FormatterPrefsBridgeSource (Live/InMemory) -> ...Model (no view HTTP).
  setGlobalLocale / setGlobalPrecision  -> FormatterPrefsBridgeApplier over FormatterPrefsBridgeStore (process-wide,
    getGlobalLocale / getGlobalPrecision     OSAllocatedUnfairLock-guarded; the numberFormat module-globals parity:
                                             empty->en-US, clamp [0,20], en-US/2 defaults). Default applier = shared.
  resolveLocale(settings.locale)        -> FormatterPrefsBridgeLocale.resolve (verbatim: original tag when trimmed
                                             non-empty, else "en-US") + .isExplicit (the applied-vs-defaults decider).
  settings.decimal_precision ?? 2       -> Config.defaultPrecision (2); 0 is treated as an explicit user choice.
  subscribe(TOPICS.SETTINGS_CHANGED)    -> FormatterPrefsBridgeBroadcast (NotificationCenter "io.teslasync.settings
    -> qc.invalidateQueries(['settings'])    .changed") -> model.refresh() (the native refetch).
  render null (anonymous, invisible)    -> P4 leaf "never a blank box": a compact, accessible diagnostic of the two
                                             values the bridge syncs (locale + decimal precision), across all states.
  i18n                                  -> every string via FormatterPrefsBridgeStrings (P1/S10); web contributes no
                                             t() keys, so all keys are native P4 chrome with English fallbacks.
  telemetry                             -> view.opened surface="FormatterPrefsBridge" once on appear (P1/S11).
  Reduce Motion                         -> TSFadeIn + TSSkeleton shimmer honour accessibilityReduceMotion.

  Parity decision (logged, no silent drift): the web effect always applies the resolved values (it runs whenever
  `settings` resolves), so the native model applies in BOTH resolved phases — `applied` AND `usingDefaults` — and
  a unit test pins that the en-US/2 defaults are written. The web de-dupe (compare against last-written AND current
  global; record-without-write on first resolve) is reproduced verbatim and pinned by ModelApplyTests. The web
  passes the RAW precision to setGlobalPrecision (which clamps); the native Store clamps identically, so the
  apply/de-dupe matches even for out-of-range inputs (asserted in StoreTests).

STATES (every web side effect + P4 leaf state reproduced — never a hidden/blank surface)
  loading        : skeleton card chrome (the `['settings']` query in flight).
  unavailable    : retry tile (web QueryError peer; the query-failure branch — a P4 leaf state).
  usingDefaults  : friendly "device defaults" card (native parity of resolveLocale('')->en-US + decimal_precision
                   ?? 2 taking effect with nothing configured — the web invisible null, made informative).
  applied        : active locale + decimal-precision card (the prefs the bridge syncs).
  stale          : freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the rising edge.
  offline        : freshness chip over the cached prefs (no auto-refresh while offline).
  Each state has a #if DEBUG preview + a unit test.

